    },
    {
      "id": 28, "type": "bargauge", "title": "Procedure p95 at selected load", "description": "Nearest-rank p95 of condition-level p95 procedure latency. With only three repetitions this equals the maximum repetition and is not a stable production tail estimate.", "gridPos": {"h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 68},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "targets": [{"refId": "A", "expr": "cn5g_performance_reviewed_procedure_latency_seconds{ue_level=\"$ue_level\",estimator=\"condition_p95\",statistic=\"p95_nearest_rank\"}", "instant": true, "legendFormat": "{{procedure}}"}],
      "fieldConfig": {"defaults": {"unit": "s", "min": 0, "color": {"mode": "continuous-YlRd"}}, "overrides": []},
      "options": {"displayMode": "gradient", "orientation": "horizontal", "showUnfilled": true, "valueMode": "color", "reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "values": false}}
    },
    {
      "id": 29, "type": "text", "title": "Scope and publication limits", "gridPos": {"h": 5, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 77},
      "options": {"mode": "markdown", "content": "### What these panels do **not** claim\nThis was one Ubuntu host, one kind node, Open5GS, and a user-space UERANSIM radio model. It is not carrier capacity, public-cloud sizing, high availability, or physical-layer performance. Reverse TCP and UDP were fixed service-load checks. Three repetitions support descriptive medians and ranges; nearest-rank p95 equals the maximum observation and must not be presented as a stable tail distribution. Failed exploratory campaigns remain excluded from every displayed value."}
    }
  ]
}
